# Universal Doc-to-Calendar Rule (`doc-to-calendar`)

When the user asks to extract dates, deadlines, exams, meetings, itineraries, or schedules from a document (PDF, DOCX, TXT, MD, CSV, HTML, ICS), **an image/screenshot** (PNG, JPG, WEBP), or **pasted text/notes**:

1. **Detect Mode**:
   - **`quick` mode** (`quick`, `--quick`, `"fast"`, `"auto"`): Skip clarification questions. Auto-apply optimal defaults (All key events, shortened tags `DDL`/`XM`/`MTG`/`LEC`/`HOL`/`FLIGHT`, `23:59` for date-only deadlines, All-Day for date-only holidays/events, smart alarms `-P1D`/`-PT2H` for deadlines and `-PT30M` for meetings, auto-detected timezone). Immediately generate `.ics` (and push to Google Calendar if `gcal` was requested).
   - **Standard mode**: Ask one compact clarification batch covering scope, cohorts/tracks (if ambiguous), missing times, category labels, alarms, short code, filename, AND **Google Calendar options** (`.ics` vs. direct Google Calendar sync vs. both, existing vs. new calendar, and per-category colors 1–11).
2. **Format Titles**:
   `[SHORT CODE - ]CATEGORY - Event Title`
3. **Generate RFC 5545 `.ics` File**:
   `python scripts/generate_ics.py -i <json_file> -o <filename>.ics`
4. **Optional Direct Google Calendar Push**:
   - Inspect calendars: `python scripts/push_to_gcalendar.py --list-calendars`
   - Push with per-category colors: `python scripts/push_to_gcalendar.py -i <json_file> --cal "<id_or_name>" --color-map "DDL=11,EXAM=4,LEC=9,HOL=2"`
5. **Deliver Preview & Links**: Display the Markdown staging table, link any `.ics` file, and share Google Calendar event links.
